WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.015
It was a normal day for Leo.

00:00:02.015 --> 00:00:04.537
He opened his furniture shop, straightened the

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.050
display, and waited.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.563
People hurried past.

00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:09.265
One checked their phone.

00:00:09.265 --> 00:00:11.282
Another glanced at the window and kept

00:00:11.282 --> 00:00:12.165
walking.

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:13.867
Days went by, but the shop stayed

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:14.623
quiet.

00:00:14.623 --> 00:00:16.577
Leo had data everywhere, yet he still

00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:18.342
couldn't tell who to reach or what

00:00:18.342 --> 00:00:19.225
to offer.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.225
Could AI do this for Leo?

00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:25.147
Meet Market Metro: a simulated commerce environment

00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:28.174
where AI agents analyze shopper behavior, train

00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:31.053
models, and test marketing campaigns.

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:34.153
We measure how those decisions change purchases,

00:00:34.153 --> 00:00:37.475
merchant contribution, and PayPal payments.

00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:40.345
An ontology is the shared map underneath.

00:00:40.345 --> 00:00:43.338
It connects shoppers, products and payments, routes

00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:46.332
recommendations and inquiries to the right training

00:00:46.332 --> 00:00:48.395
data, and keeps later outcomes out of

00:00:48.395 --> 00:00:49.592
model inputs.

00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:52.942
Now follow one saved reactivation campaign.

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:56.042
The agent analyzes demand, chooses twenty eight

00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:58.792
days of history, and fits two models.

00:00:58.867 --> 00:01:00.967
A verifier tests the campaign before it

00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:02.342
reaches shoppers.

00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:04.083
The first idea doesn't get a free

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.058
pass.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.683
A verifier tests both rankings in separate

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.983
development markets and selects the one that

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:12.558
earns more while protecting merchants.

00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.408
On day thirty five, the selected recommendation

00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:16.983
reaches our shopper.

00:01:17.058 --> 00:01:18.883
They buy a ninety six dollar side

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:21.323
table, and it arrives the next day;

00:01:21.398 --> 00:01:24.523
fixed rules left that same request unfilled.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.984
We mirror that order once through PayPal

00:01:26.984 --> 00:01:27.944
Sandbox.

00:01:27.944 --> 00:01:30.347
The completed capture records the fee and

00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:33.092
merchant proceeds, then returns a receipt that

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.670
links all the way back to the

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:35.700
purchase.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.763
Against fixed rules, sixteen more purchases were

00:01:38.763 --> 00:01:40.359
completed and kept.

00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.994
That's two thousand three hundred forty five

00:01:42.994 --> 00:01:45.283
dollars in extra payment volume, over a

00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:48.196
thousand dollars in merchant contribution, and a

00:01:48.196 --> 00:01:50.901
hundred fifteen dollars in modeled PayPal net

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.150
after AI cost.

00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:54.471
Judges can follow the whole trail in

00:01:54.471 --> 00:01:56.439
A G Grid, from model training and

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:59.137
the agent's decision to the PayPal receipt,

00:01:59.137 --> 00:02:01.908
instead of taking the result on trust.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.925
Market Metro turns observed activity into tested

00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:08.700
campaigns and traceable payments: agentic commerce that

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.575
learns.
